---
// Decorative dot-matrix map of the province of Ontario: land only (the Great
// Lakes are cut out), 917 dots on a regular grid. Built from Natural Earth
// 1:50m admin-1 and lakes (public domain), rasterised to a 4.348-unit grid.
// Every dot is the same gold (--cell-gold, set per cell by Trust.astro: a deeper
// wood mix on light cells for contrast, plain --color-accent on dark ones).
// Dots on the outer rim and around the lakes (any of the 8 grid neighbours
// missing) are drawn smaller, r 1.0 against 1.35. The Durham / Peterborough dot is not special-cased.
// Purely decorative.
// Dots are real <circle>s on purpose: zero-length round-cap path segments are
// dropped by some browsers once the layer is composited.
---

